Let $\quad z=x+i y\therefore \arg \left(\frac{z-2}{z+2}\right)=\frac{\pi}{3}\begin{aligned} &amp; \Rightarrow \arg (z-2)-\arg (z+2)=\frac{\pi}{3} \\ &amp; \Rightarrow \arg ((x-2)+i y)-\arg ((x+2)+i y)=\frac{\pi}{3} \\ &amp; \Rightarrow \quad \tan ^{-1}\left(\frac{y}{x-2}\right)-\tan ^{-1}\left(\frac{y}{x+2}\right)=\frac{\pi}{3}\end{aligned}\begin{array}{ll}\Rightarrow \quad &amp; \tan ^{-1}\left[\frac{\frac{y}{x-2}-\frac{y}{x+2}}{1+\frac{y}{x-2} \times \frac{y}{x+2}}\right]=\frac{\pi}{3} \\ \Rightarrow &amp; {\left[\frac{4 y}{x^2-4+y^2}\right]=\tan \frac{\pi}{3}=\sqrt{3}}\end{array}
\begin{array}{ll}
\Rightarrow$&amp; x²-4+y²=$\frac{4 y}{\sqrt{3}}$\\
\Rightarrow &amp; x²+y²-$\frac{4 y}{\sqrt{3}}-$4=0
\end{array}
Hence, it represents a equation of circle.
